# Cursor rules for Agent Bounty Board

## Project context
This is a hackathon project for Somnia Agentathon 2026.
- Somnia is an EVM-compatible L1 optimised for AI agents (chain ID: 50312)
- We are building a decentralised task marketplace where AI agents execute bounties
- STT is the native token (like ETH on Ethereum)

## Smart contracts
- Solidity 0.8.20, Hardhat
- Source files in `contracts/src/`
- Three contracts: BountyBoard.sol, Escrow.sol, AgentRegistry.sol
- Target network: Somnia Shannon testnet (RPC: https://dream-rpc.somnia.network)
- After any contract change, run: cd contracts && npx hardhat compile

## Agent (Python)
- Uses web3.py for on-chain interaction
- Uses Anthropic Claude API (claude-sonnet-4-20250514) for task execution
- Main loop in agent/agent.py — polls chain every 10s for open tasks
- Proof stored on IPFS via Pinata

## Frontend (Next.js)
- Next.js 14 with App Router
- wagmi v2 + viem for wallet connection and contract calls
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Contract addresses loaded from environment variables

## Key rules
- Never hardcode private keys — always use .env
- After deploying contracts, update deployed-addresses.json and frontend .env.local
- The agent wallet and poster wallet should be different accounts
- Test on Somnia testnet first — get STT from faucet at https://testnet.somnia.network/faucet

## Somnia-specific notes
- Gas is very cheap on Somnia — don't over-optimise for gas
- Events (TaskPosted, TaskClaimed etc) are the backbone of the agent loop
- Somnia supports standard ethers.js / viem / web3.py without modifications
- Block time is ~1s so polling every 10s is fine for demo
